e><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133057312,imgsize-680607.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A moth outbreak has killed off forests across Siberia, now the flammable wood is causing wildfires]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133025037.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a catastrophic turn of events, a diminutive moth has decimated vast stretches of Siberian forest, transforming them into a fire hazard of monumental proportions. The Siberian silk moth's caterpillar stage ravages tree needles, resulting in widespread die-offs over several years. Major outbreaks have persisted over the decades, decimating millions of hectares, and now this ecological calamity aligns with an urgent wildfire emergency that has meteorological implications.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/a-moth-outbreak-has-killed-off-forests-across-siberia-now-the-flammable-wood-is-causing-wildfires-that-humans-are-unable-to-contain/articleshow/133025037.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/a-moth-outbreak-has-killed-off-forests-across-siberia-now-the-flammable-wood-is-causing-wildfires-that-humans-are-unable-to-contain/articleshow/133025037.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T23:03:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133027019,imgsize-150807.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida's millions of dumped tyres are still being cleaned up 50 years later]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133054530.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Florida is set to embark on an ambitious initiative to clear millions of old tires that were dumped offshore decades ago. Initially forming an artificial reef, these tires have since led to significant damage to natural coral ecosystems. Present surveys indicate that over half a million tires still litter thousands of acres.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-dumped-millions-of-tyres-into-the-ocean-to-build-a-reef-more-than-50-years-later-it-is-still-cleaning-them-up/articleshow/133054530.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-dumped-millions-of-tyres-into-the-ocean-to-build-a-reef-more-than-50-years-later-it-is-still-cleaning-them-up/articleshow/133054530.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T20:06:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133054605,imgsize-124813.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Death of PhD student Vikram Mubayi after California hike leaves family seeking answers]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133057756.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/he-did-not-make-it-death-of-phd-student-vikram-mubayi-after-california-hike-leaves-family-seeking-answers/articleshow/133057756.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/he-did-not-make-it-death-of-phd-student-vikram-mubayi-after-california-hike-leaves-family-seeking-answers/articleshow/133057756.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T23:34:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133057756,imgsize-222550.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Inside Portugal’s 19th-century goat tower, where dwarf goats climb a spiral ramp]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133056289.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/inside-portugals-19th-century-goat-tower-where-dwarf-goats-climb-a-spiral-ramp-to-a-three-storey-home/articleshow/133056289.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/inside-portugals-19th-century-goat-tower-where-dwarf-goats-climb-a-spiral-ramp-to-a-three-storey-home/articleshow/133056289.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T22:52:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133056535,imgsize-50458.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Costa Rica's tiny 'coffee frog,' a nocturnal species found living among coffee shrubs]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133055805.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A remarkable discovery in Costa Rica reveals a diminutive nocturnal frog inhabiting the coffee plantations. Measuring less than four centimeters, this unique species relies on small insects for food and foliage for protection. Essential to its lifecycle are local streams, which face risks from pesticide runoff. This finding not only emphasizes the rich biodiversity in agricultural settings but also the urgent need for conservation initiatives.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-costa-ricas-tiny-coffee-frog-a-nocturnal-species-found-living-among-coffee-shrubs/articleshow/133055805.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-costa-ricas-tiny-coffee-frog-a-nocturnal-species-found-living-among-coffee-shrubs/articleshow/133055805.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T22:17:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133055926,imgsize-1923856.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[2-year-old sister becomes perfect bone marrow match for Utah girl with aplastic anemia]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133055066.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Emma Meline, a young girl diagnosed with severe aplastic anemia right before Christmas, found hope in her little sister Lucy. At only two years old, Lucy bravely became a bone marrow donor, granting Emma the chance for a life-saving transplant. After a challenging journey, Emma celebrated her fifth birthday at home, marking a remarkable recovery. This profound experience deepened the unbreakable bond between the two sisters.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/utah-girl-emma-meline-was-diagnosed-with-severe-aplastic-anemia-days-before-christmas-her-2-year-old-sister-became-her-perfect-bone-marrow-match/articleshow/133055066.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/utah-girl-emma-meline-was-diagnosed-with-severe-aplastic-anemia-days-before-christmas-her-2-year-old-sister-became-her-perfect-bone-marrow-match/articleshow/133055066.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T21:00:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133055176,imgsize-979312.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Dinosaur bone found in 1999 finally identified as 3-metre species after 27 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133054574.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[htt